# Frontend Rule

Use React with TypeScript and small composable components.

Requirements:
- Use named interfaces/types for component props.
- Use lucide-react for icons.
- Use Tailwind utility classes.
- Use Framer Motion only for meaningful microinteractions.
- Include loading, empty, and error states.
- Keep all pages responsive from 390px mobile width through desktop.
- Avoid large, hardcoded text blocks in components; store constants in data or lib files.
- Use aria-label on icon-only buttons.
- Do not use color alone to communicate status.
- Keep user-facing copy calm, concise, and non-alarmist.
- Every peer-match screen must include a visible leave or report option.
